  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1272281,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "You awaken disoriented within a sprawling, labyrinthine complex – the Chronarium. Time itself is fractured here, and you are trapped within a repeating fifteen-second loop. Each cycle resets your progress, but with each iteration, fragments of memory return, revealing clues to your identity and the nature of your imprisonment.\n\n*15 Seconds Multiple Copy V1.9* for Commodore 64 plunges you into this mind-bending puzzle adventure. Explore detailed chambers, interact with cryptic entities, and decipher environmental puzzles that shift subtly with each loop. Your actions in one cycle directly impact subsequent loops – a moved object might be found elsewhere next time, or a conversation altered by your previous choices.\n\nMaster the fifteen-second window to observe, plan, and execute. Experimentation is key; what seems insignificant at first may hold the key to breaking free.  The game features multiple endings dependent on your actions and discoveries. Can you unravel the mysteries of the Chronarium before time consumes you? Prepare for a challenging and rewarding experience that tests your observation skills and memory in this unique, time-bending adventure!"
    },
